---
source: crates/surfaces/cli/src/main.rs
expression: command.clone().render_long_help().to_string()
---
Validate .spec files and report diagnostics

Usage: specforge check [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --path <PATH>
          A path inside the project (the nearest directory at or above it holding specforge.json; none: the directory itself, with the default configuration)
          
          [default: .]

      --strict
          Promote warnings to errors

      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format: human or json (json with --pick)
          
          [default: human]
          [possible values: human, json]

      --pick <PATH>
          Print only the values at this path of the command's JSON answer, one per line, e.g. '.[code=E003].message' on check or '.extensions[].settings[name=<setting>].value' on settings. The path is steps: `.key`, `[n]` (digits, no leading zero), `[]` (every item) and `[<key>=<value>]` (the items whose field <key> is <value>, e.g. `[kind=plan]`: <key> may be dotted, `[fields.result=issue]`, and a number, boolean or null is compared as JSON, `[fields.backlog=true]`, `[fields.wave=2]`; an object or array is never selected); a `.` before `[` may be left out, and `.` alone is the whole answer. One line per value reached: a string bare (a newline in it is printed as is), an integer as is and any other number as an f64 (`1.0`, `-0.0`, `1e3` as `1000.0`), a boolean, object or array as compact JSON; null or a missing value prints nothing, and is not an error. It implies --format json (--format human is refused): errors print as they do under json, and the exit code is the command's.

      --lint <LINT>
          Extra lint profiles: inferred (I200/I202 from specforge-infer.json); pedantic is the default and adds nothing
          
          [possible values: inferred, pedantic]

      --severity <SEVERITY>
          Show only diagnostics of this severity (after --strict); the exit code still judges everything reported
          
          [possible values: error, warning, info]

      --since <REV>
          Judge immutable and append-only history against the merge-base of this git revision and HEAD

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
